speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise on a matter of urgent and pressing necessity. On Tuesday, December 23, 1975, the Prime Minister in a television conversation with Bruce Phillips and Carole Taylor said, and I quote;
In the first half of this year, for instance, the public sector salaries have grown by something like 22 per cent as against 14 per cent in the private sector because in the private sector there is a limit that's called bankruptcy. In the public sector there's not, so we obviously have to change that.
The change introduced by the Prime Minister is called the Anti-Inflation Board. The Financial Times-
